<title>AUSTRALIA: ATHLETICS-GEORGE BREAKS WOMEN'S POLE VAULT WORLD RECORD.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-GEORGE BREAKS WOMEN'S POLE VAULT WORLD RECORD.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's Emma George broke her own pole vault world record at the Victoria state track and field championships.</p>
<p>She cleared 4.50 metres on Saturday to add five centimetres to the mark she set a meeting in Japan last July.</p>
<p>It was the eighth time George had set a world mark since November 1995.</p>
